<article class="about-content">
  <header class="section-header">
    <p class="section-kicker">About Live</p>
    <h1>A peek inside my digital sketchbook.</h1>
    <p>Live is where I keep notes on work that is still taking shape and document my ideas and process.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="about-prose">
    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>I make websites, tools, games and other things, often with the help of generative tools. I use Live to record what I tried, what worked, and what I changed my mind about.</p>
    <p>There is plenty of commentary about AI. I want to keep a practical record of what using it to make things is actually like.</p>

    <h2>What appears here</h2>
    <p>Updates on things I’m making, useful discoveries, things I decide not to pursue, and questions I haven’t answered yet. These are notes from the work rather than polished essays.</p>

    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <p>While I use generative tools to test my ideas and build things quickly, I’m less of a fan of using them to articulate my thoughts and experiences. I try and keep the words you read here my own. I’ve written more about my thinking in <a href="https://anthonycreates.com/writing/on-writing-and-ai/">On Writing and AI</a>.</p>
    <p>When I include words produced by a model, they are labelled “From the model” and set apart visually. Everything else is my own writing, apart from corrections to spelling and grammar.</p>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>Anyone interested in making things, or finding their way back to their own creativity. I hope something here is useful, encouraging or simply interesting.</p>
  </div>
</article>
